{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1795360950,"nonce":"q2R2HfGXgYLBmsQ4mHdqiC71isQ=","target":"736654d5588b9cb3e8512e5c09af3decce319aa2d35640887f05afcc58cdad2c","message":"`jno.precond.hypre(kind=\"ams\")` landed in `f4ec3961` on `fem/maxwell-av` as a **reference-grade**\nH(curl) preconditioner via PETSc. It works and is tested, but three things about it are deliberately\nunfinished, and one measurement suggests the interesting work is elsewhere.\n\n\nOn the 89,920-DOF H(curl) block of an A–V system with layered windings:\n\n| | relative residual |\n| --- | --- |\n| hypre AMS | 4.33e-09 |\n| jNO's own `ams()` | 8.03e-09 |\n\nEquivalent. jNO's AMS implementation is fine. The value of the backend is as an **oracle** — it is\nhow the σ=0 cliff below was found — and for the semidefinite machinery jNO lacks.\n\n\n`jno/utils/solver/ams.py` has `discrete_gradient` (G) and `nodal_vector_interpolation` (Π) — the\ndefinite case only. hypre additionally carries, for σ=0 over part of the domain: interior-node\nmarking, a restricted gradient G₀, δ·G₀ᵀG₀ regularisation, and periodic projection onto ker(G₀ᵀ).\nMeasured where that matters: **8.6e-03 with interior nodes marked, no progress at all without**.\n\n**But it is probably not worth implementing.** A σ floor of 1e-6 S/m in the air (1.7e-14 × copper,\nphysics verified unchanged) takes plain AMS from *no progress* to **16 iterations** — and the\ninterior-node path was strictly *worse* in every σ\u003e0 case tested. The cliff is at exactly zero.\n\n\n1. **Host round-trip per apply.** `pure_callback` per iteration, not traceable. Does not affect\n   differentiability (`custom_linear_solve` differentiates the operator, never the preconditioner —\n   same contract as SuperLU/PARDISO/pyamg), but it caps throughput.\n2. **`petsc4py` is an undeclared optional dependency.** Import failure raises with an install hint;\n   it is not in `pyproject`, and there is no CI coverage, so `tests/test_precond_hypre.py` skips\n   silently where it is absent.\n3. **Only `kind` and `-pc_hypre_\u003ckind\u003e_\u003ckey\u003e` options are plumbed.** `setHYPREAMSSetInteriorNodes`,\n   `SetBetaPoissonMatrix` and `SetEdgeConstantVectors` are reachable from petsc4py but not exposed —\n   deliberately, since the σ floor made them unnecessary here.\n\n\nFor the A–V system the *inner* problem (K+M) takes **15 iterations**; the *outer* complex solve takes\n**~4000** and 103.6 s, even though it converges to the correct answer. Two obvious fixes are already\nruled out by measurement: `ams().build(fem, field=u)` (the default already factors once per solve,\nand inside `real_equivalent` a build freezes *complex* auxiliaries and applies them to the *real*\nK+M — the bug `190890ed` fixed), and the device-resident `ams(aux=amg())`, which **fails to converge**\nhere at 3.4e-02 where the exact host auxiliary converges. What is needed is a better preconditioner\nfor the **complex** system — `real_equivalent`'s K+M approximation is weak for this operator — not a\nfaster inner.","files":null}]}